winewayland: only force the foreground for focus arriving from OUTSIDE the process

Premiere's Program Monitor fullscreen was deaf to ordinary keys. Escape would not leave
fullscreen, space would not play -- but Ctrl+Q still quit the app. Reported as "Escape does not
exit fullscreen"; it is actually every ordinary key.

CAUSE. KWin sends wl_keyboard.enter whenever a surface takes keyboard focus, INCLUDING when focus
moves between two of the application's own windows. keyboard_handle_enter() turned every one of
those into WM_WAYLAND_SET_FOREGROUND -> NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(). For an in-app move
that overrides activation the application has just performed itself, and Premiere's key routing is
left pointing where it was before we intervened. Accelerators survive because they are dispatched
from the message loop and never depend on which window is active -- which is exactly why Ctrl+Q
worked and made the keyboard path look healthy.

The deactivation handler already asks this question and skips in-app changes ("SKIP (in-app focus
change)"). The enter path never did. The two were asymmetric; this makes them agree.

FIX: post the foreground only when the current foreground window does NOT belong to this process.
External activation (clicking in from another application, alt-tab) is unaffected; in-app focus
moves are left to the app.

MEASURED. Before: keys dead on every fullscreen entry, in-app clicks do NOT repair it, only
clicking another application and back does -- i.e. only a full WM_ACTIVATEAPP cycle. After: keys
work immediately with no click, and normal activation still works (operator-verified: clicking in
from another app, switching between Premiere windows, dialogs, menus).

⭐ HOW IT WAS FOUND, because six theories died first. The report ruled out delivery, routing and
focus churn, all correctly. What actually discriminated was cheap and behavioural:
  * SPACE also does nothing -- so it is not an Escape bug, it is every window-routed key, and
    accelerators are the exception that names the mechanism.
  * an IN-APP click does NOT repair it while leaving the app and returning does -- which said the
    repair needs WM_ACTIVATEAPP, and pointed straight at activation rather than input.
  * +msg showed the difference between the two activations: entry produces a lone WM_NCACTIVATE,
    the click produces WM_ACTIVATEAPP 0 then 1.
⛔ Dead ends, each disproven with the gate PROVEN to have taken effect, not assumed: foreground
loss to the desktop (that DEACTIVATING line is the operator's own click-away), the 1 px
coords_to_window rounding, monitor geometry, SWP_NOSIZE suppressing WM_SIZE, and raw input (the
app does not use it -- zero +rawinput lines).

⚠️ STILL OPEN, separate bugs measured alongside this one:
  1. The FIRST fullscreen entry is oversized (self-corrects on the next entry, or on play).
     Independent of this fix.
  2. Win32 reports DISPLAY2 as 3260x1834 @ (6520,270) when it is 1920x1080 -- size scaled by the
     primary monitor's DPI, origin scaled TWICE. The known mixed-per-monitor-DPI bug, now with
     exact numbers.
  3. After clicking back into the app, clicking a panel highlights its border then immediately
     deselects it. Noticed in the same session as this change and NOT yet established as
     pre-existing -- treat as possibly introduced here until checked.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
@@ -827,8 +827,55 @@
          * skip the SetForegroundWindow post for it (compositor keyboard focus alone is
          * harmless — the app just never wanted this popup to become the active window). */
         DWORD ex_style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE);
+
+        /* NEUTRON: only force the foreground for focus arriving from OUTSIDE this process.
+         *
+         * KWin sends wl_keyboard.enter whenever a surface takes keyboard focus -- including when
+         * the focus merely moves between two of the application's OWN windows. Forcing
+         * SetForegroundWindow for those in-app moves overrides activation the app has just
+         * performed itself, and the app's key routing is left pointing at whatever it had chosen
+         * before we intervened.
+         *
+         * MEASURED 2026-08-31 on Premiere: entering the Program Monitor's fullscreen leaves the
+         * fullscreen window deaf to ORDINARY keys (space, escape) while accelerators (Ctrl+Q) keep
+         * working, because accelerators are dispatched from the message loop and never depend on
+         * which window is active. Keys were provably delivered to the correct window the whole
+         * time. Clicking another application and back fixed it; clicking inside Premiere did not --
+         * i.e. only a full WM_ACTIVATEAPP cycle repaired it. With this post suppressed the keys
+         * work immediately, with no click.
+         *
+         * The deactivation handler already asks exactly this question and skips in-app changes
+         * ("SKIP (in-app focus change)"); the enter path never did, so the two were asymmetric.
+         *
+         * Kill switch: NEUTRON_KBD_FOREGROUND=0 suppresses the post entirely (the probe that
+         * identified this); NEUTRON_KBD_FOREGROUND=2 restores the old unconditional behaviour. */
         if (surface->window.managed && !(ex_style & WS_EX_NOACTIVATE))
-            NtUserPostMessage(hwnd, WM_WAYLAND_SET_FOREGROUND, 0, 0);
+        {
+            static int mode = -1;
+            HWND fg;
+            DWORD fg_pid = 0;
+
+            if (mode < 0)
+            {
+                const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_KBD_FOREGROUND");
+                mode = e ? atoi(e) : 1;
+            }
+
+            fg = NtUserGetForegroundWindow();
+            if (fg) NtUserGetWindowThread(fg, &fg_pid);
+
+            if (mode == 0)
+                ERR("neutron-kbdfg: hwnd=%p SKIP (probe: post disabled)\n", hwnd);
+            else if (mode != 2 && fg_pid == GetCurrentProcessId())
+                ERR("neutron-kbdfg: hwnd=%p SKIP -- foreground %p is already ours, this is an "
+                    "in-app focus change and the app owns its own activation\n", hwnd, fg);
+            else
+            {
+                ERR("neutron-kbdfg: hwnd=%p FOREGROUNDING (focus arrived from outside; fg=%p)\n",
+                    hwnd, fg);
+                NtUserPostMessage(hwnd, WM_WAYLAND_SET_FOREGROUND, 0, 0);
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
